.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-config - Manage persisted CLI defaults (base-url, chain, token, output, http-timeout)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 config [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage persisted CLI defaults stored in the config file.

.PP
Run bare to list the settings in effect, with each value and where it comes from:
a flag, an env var, the config file, or the built-in default (base-url, chain and
token have one, so they are always listed; admin-url, output and http-timeout only
once set). Resolution precedence is: flag  >  env var  >  config file  >  default.

.PP
A stored default fills in the matching flag when you omit it, so the chain and the
token can be set once instead of on every command: 'config set chain arc' and
\&'config set token USDC' make every payment command use them until you pass -c/-t.
\&'config unset' removes your value and the built-in default applies again.

.PP
Addresses and signing keys are NOT settable here: use the alias book ('rail0 aliases
add') and the OS keychain ('rail0 keys add', passed as @name), which already spare
you the retyping without making the parties or the signer implicit.

.PP
Settable keys (env var) — and what the CLI does when the key is not set:
  admin-url     Admin app URL that 'rail0 open' opens (RAIL0_ADMIN_URL) — not set: the matching flag must be passed
  base-url      RAIL0 gateway base URL (RAIL0_BASE_URL) — not set: the CLI uses https://api.rail0.xyz
  chain         Default chain for --chain/-c: a slug (arc) or a chain id (RAIL0_CHAIN) — not set: the matching flag must be passed
  chain-id      Legacy numeric default chain; superseded by chain (RAIL0_CHAIN_ID) — not set: the matching flag must be passed
  http-timeout  Per-request HTTP timeout in seconds (RAIL0_HTTP_TIMEOUT) — not set: the CLI uses 30
  output        Default output mode: auto, json, pretty or quiet (RAIL0_OUTPUT) — not set: the CLI uses auto
  token         Default token symbol for --token/-t (e.g. USDC) (RAIL0_TOKEN_SYMBOL) — not set: the matching flag must be passed


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for config


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 config
  rail0 config set chain arc
  rail0 config set token USDC
  rail0 config get chain
  rail0 config unset chain
  rail0 config set output pretty
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-get(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-path(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-set(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-unset(1)\fP
